		note {
			value """
Comments on "Joseph Tag Torture-Mary First Jones" FAMILY Record.

This record contains all possible types of data that can be stored in a FAMILY (FAM) GEDCOM record. Here are some comments on the data tested here and things to look for when this file is imported into any GEDCOM application:

1. The marriage event (MARR) uses all possible tags for such a structure including notes, sources, and a link to a multimedia file.

2. This family has two children.

3. This family has all possible family events (including a generic event or EVEN structure). Some notes are:
     a. The engaged structure has all possible tags for event detail.
     b. The annulment event (ANUL) has no data except a "Y" in the first line to indicate that the event has occurred. The importing software should keep this event in this record even though it contains no data.
     c. The LDS Spouse Sealing event tests all possible detail tags for an LDS.
     d. The TYPE tag of each event has the name of the GEDCOM tag for that event. There is no TYPE tag in the annulment event because that structure is empty.

4. This record has this one note structure which is to a set of embedded notes (and which you are reading now).

5. This record has one source citation.

6. This record is linked a submitter.

7. This record has all remaining tags allowed in FAMILY records for user reference number, record ID, and the changed date."""
			audit {
				creation {
					date 2026-08-26T00:00:00Z
					comment From GEDCOM conversion
				}
			}
		}
		name {
			text {
				value Family of Joseph and Mary First
			}
		}
		source {
			source S25
		}
	}

